{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The REMOTE arm of chat_llm: the peer IS the transport - no HTTP, no keys, no dialect here. The whole (messages, tools) pair goes to the named peer (LLM_REMOTE=<peer-uuid>) via app.app.exec, which runs its OWN chat_llm under its own LLM= arm and answers in this command's normalized shape, passed through untouched (tools, vision, thinking blocks survive because nothing is re-rendered). Oversized conversations split across sequential service-exec frames (LLM_REMOTE_SPLIT=on); LLM_REMOTE_ID overrides the far chat_llm command id. Peer chaining resolves at wherever an HTTP arm is set. Helpers from llm_common. Internal: the public entry point is agent.llm.chat_llm.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\nuse crate::agent::llm::llm_common::*;","params":[],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"pktyxy1a0f76c2dddj175","readers":[],"time":1790865968012,"username":"system","writers":[]}